.SH A) OVERVIEW
yPARSE_stds will cover the standard input/output field specifications and
how they are defined.  while being exact might be fun, generalizing field
types allows a great deal of low complexity, shared usage.

.SH B) RECORD SPECIFICATION
each field specification is a single letter and a record specification is
then an ordered string of field letters.

.nf
ex, for gyges
  --  ---name---- -spec--  cnt   ----translated fields------------------
   1  tabs·········LTcTTc···6····LABEL, TERSE, char, TERSE, TERSE, char
   2  width········Tss······3····TERSE, short, short
   3  height·······Tss······3····TERSE, short, short
   4  free cells···TTO······3····TERSE, TERSE, remainder
   5  dep cells····TTO······3····TERSE, TERSE, remainder

.SH C) NUMERIC FIELDS
there are 14 standard numeric field specifications.  if you what something
more specific, simply print to a string and output that to an an appropriately
long string field.

.SS character
c      char            

.SS integers
s      short            3    ¬                 -99 to 999                  ¬
i      int              6    ¬             -999999 to 999999               ¬
l      llong           10    ¬          -999999999 to 9999999999           ¬
h      huge llong      16    ¬    -999999999999998 to 9999999999999998     ¬

.SS integers with commas
,      comma int       10    ¬          -9,999,999 to 99,999,999           ¬
;      comma llong     19    ¬ -99,999,999,999,999 to 999,999,999,999,999  ¬

.SS floats
k      kinematics      6/1   ¬              -999.9 to 9999.9               ¬
f      float           8/2   ¬            -9999.99 to 99999.99             ¬
d      double         10/3   ¬          -99999.999 to 999999.999           ¬
t      technical      18/6   ¬  -9999999999.999999 to 99999999999.999999   ¬

.SS exponential format
e      s.exponent      2/3   ¬
m      m.exponent      2.7   ¬
b      b.exponent      2/12  ¬

.SH D) STRING FIELDS
there are 15 standard string field specifications.  if you want something more
specific just round up and trim later.

.SS character
C      char            1.1s

.SS short
S      LEN_SHORT       5.5s
T      LEN_TERSE      10.10s
U      LEN_USER       12.12s
L      LEN_LABEL      20.20s

.SS medium
3      LEN_TITLE      30.30s
4      40             40.40s
D      LEN_DESC       50.50s
6      60             60.60s
7      70             70.70s
8      80             80.80s

.SS long
H      LEN_HUND      100.100s
F      LEN_FULL      200.200s
R      LEN_RECD     2000.2000s
O      all remaining

.SH E) SKIPPING
-      skip field
